    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0847" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg719"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 541.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19, 1885</date>.
                        (Received July 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 327.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your numbers 327 and 346,
                    relating to the case of Mr. F. B. Hamel against the custom-house at Barcelona, I
                    have to report that I have executed your instructions by addressing a note to
                    the <pb facs="0848" n="720" xml:id="pg720"/> minister of state, of which a copy
                    is herewith inclosed. When I shall have notice that my note and its inclosures
                    have been sent to the minister of finance, I will seek a personal interview with
                    the latter minister to press the case upon his favorable consideration.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d541-a1.xml" xpointer="d541-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
